---
title: OpenTelemetry
id: otel
order: 3
description: "Emit vendor-neutral OpenTelemetry traces and metrics from every TanStack AI chat() call, following the OTel GenAI semantic conventions."
keywords:
  - tanstack ai
  - opentelemetry
  - otel
  - observability
  - tracing
  - metrics
  - gen_ai
  - semantic conventions
---
NIFT_TANSTACK_DOCUMENT_V1
{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"otelMiddleware"},{"type":"text","value":" factory wires TanStack AI into your existing OpenTelemetry setup. Every "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat()"},{"type":"text","value":" call produces a root span, one child span per provider model call (agent-loop turn "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"or"}]},{"type":"text","value":" structured-output finalization), and one grandchild span per tool call — all with "},{"type":"link","href":"https://opentelemetry.io/docs/specs/semconv/gen-ai/","children":[{"type":"text","value":"GenAI semantic-convention attributes"}]},{"type":"text","value":". It also records GenAI token and duration histograms when a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Meter"},{"type":"text","value":" is provided."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Structured-output calls with no tools skip the agent loop and only run the finalization request. That path still opens an iteration span (via the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"structuredOutput"},{"type":"text","value":" middleware phase) so backends that key off generation spans (e.g. PostHog "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"$ai_generation"},{"type":"text","value":") and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"captureContent"},{"type":"text","value":" both work. Native combined mode ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"supportsCombinedToolsAndSchema"},{"type":"text","value":") does not fire that phase — the single "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"beforeModel"},{"type":"text","value":" span covers the combined call."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"setup","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Setup"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Install "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@opentelemetry/api"},{"type":"text","value":" — it's an optional peer dependency of "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"component","name":"tabs","attributes":{"variant":"package-manager","mode":"install"},"children":[],"properties":{"data-package-manager-meta":"{\"packagesByFramework\":{\"react\":[[\"@opentelemetry/api\"]],\"vue\":[[\"@opentelemetry/api\"]],\"solid\":[[\"@opentelemetry/api\"]],\"svelte\":[[\"@opentelemetry/api\"]],\"preact\":[[\"@opentelemetry/api\"]],\"angular\":[[\"@opentelemetry/api\"]],\"vanilla\":[[\"@opentelemetry/api\"]],\"octane\":[[\"@opentelemetry/api\"]]},\"mode\":\"install\"}"}},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Wire up your OTel SDK however you already do (e.g. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@opentelemetry/sdk-node"},{"type":"text","value":"). Then pass a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Tracer"},{"type":"text","value":" (and optionally a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Meter"},{"type":"text","value":") into the middleware. The OTel middleware lives on its own subpath — importing it never affects users who don't need OTel:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { chat } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { otelMiddleware } from '@tanstack/ai/middlewares/otel'\nimport { openaiText } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\nimport { trace, metrics } from '@opentelemetry/api'\n\nconst otel = otelMiddleware({\n  tracer: trace.getTracer('my-app'),\n  meter: metrics.getMeter('my-app'),\n})\n\nconst { text } = await chat({\n  adapter: openaiText('gpt-5.5'),\n  messages: [{ role: 'user', content: 'hi' }],\n  middleware: [otel],\n  stream: false,\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"what-gets-emitted","children":[{"type":"text","value":"What gets emitted"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"spans","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Spans"}]},{"type":"code","value":"chat gpt-5.5              (root, kind: INTERNAL)\n├── chat gpt-5.5 #0       (iteration, kind: CLIENT)\n│   ├── execute_tool get_weather\n│   └── execute_tool get_time\n└── chat gpt-5.5 #1       (iteration, kind: CLIENT)","lang":"text"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Iteration spans are numbered ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"#0"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"#1"},{"type":"text","value":", ...) in the order model calls are observed, so distinct provider round-trips of the same chat are easy to pick apart in trace viewers."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"attribute-reference","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Attribute reference"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Level"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Attribute"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Value"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"root / iteration"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"gen_ai.system"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"openai"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"anthropic"},{"type":"text","value":", ..."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"iteration"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"gen_ai.operation.name"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"root / iteration"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"gen_ai.request.model"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"requested model"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"iteration"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"gen_ai.response.model"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"actual model"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"iteration"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"gen_ai.request.temperature"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"from config"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"iteration"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"gen_ai.request.top_p"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"from config"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"iteration"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"gen_ai.request.max_tokens"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"from config"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"iteration"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"gen_ai.usage.input_tokens"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"per iteration"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"iteration"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"gen_ai.usage.output_tokens"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"per iteration"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"root / iteration"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"gen_ai.usage.total_tokens"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"provider-reported total"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"root / iteration"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"gen_ai.usage.cost"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"provider-reported cost, when available"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"root / iteration"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"gen_ai.usage.cache_read.input_tokens"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"cached prompt tokens, when reported"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"root / iteration"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"gen_ai.usage.cache_creation.input_tokens"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"cache-write prompt tokens, when reported"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"root / iteration"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"gen_ai.usage.reasoning.output_tokens"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"reasoning/thinking tokens, when reported"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"root / iteration"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tanstack.ai.usage.billed_quantity"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"non-token billed quantity, when reported"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"root / iteration"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tanstack.ai.usage.billed_unit"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"unit of the billed quantity ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"seconds"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"units"},{"type":"text","value":", ...)"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"root / iteration"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tanstack.ai.usage.duration_seconds"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"deprecated duration count; read "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"billed_quantity"},{"type":"text","value":"/"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"billed_unit"},{"type":"text","value":" instead"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"root / iteration"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tanstack.ai.usage.units_billed"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"deprecated bare unit count; read "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"billed_quantity"},{"type":"text","value":"/"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"billed_unit"},{"type":"text","value":" instead"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"root / iteration"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tanstack.ai.usage.upstream_cost"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"gateway upstream cost (e.g. OpenRouter), when reported"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"root / iteration"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tanstack.ai.usage.upstream_input_cost"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"upstream input cost split, when reported"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"root / iteration"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tanstack.ai.usage.upstream_output_cost"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"upstream output cost split, when reported"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"iteration"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"gen_ai.response.finish_reasons"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"[stop]"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"[tool_calls]"},{"type":"text","value":", ..."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"root"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"gen_ai.usage.input_tokens"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"rolled up"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"root"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"gen_ai.usage.output_tokens"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"rolled up"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"root"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tanstack.ai.iterations"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"iteration count"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"tool"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"gen_ai.tool.name"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"tool name"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"tool"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"gen_ai.tool.call.id"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"tool call id"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"tool"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"gen_ai.tool.type"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"function"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"tool"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tanstack.ai.tool.outcome"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"success"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"error"}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Usage attributes beyond input/output tokens are emitted only when the provider reports them, so spans stay clean otherwise. Cache and reasoning breakdowns use the official GenAI semconv names; "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"gen_ai.usage.cost"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"gen_ai.usage.total_tokens"},{"type":"text","value":" are de-facto extensions consumed directly by backends like PostHog — without them, backends re-derive cost from their own price tables and lose cache discounts and gateway markup. Fields with no established convention (the billed quantity/unit pair, the upstream cost split, and the deprecated bare counts) are TanStack-namespaced."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For non-token billing (seconds of video or transcription, fal's endpoint units, ...), "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tanstack.ai.usage.billed_quantity"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tanstack.ai.usage.billed_unit"},{"type":"text","value":" are emitted as a pair from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"usage.billed"},{"type":"text","value":", so backends can label and aggregate media usage without knowing the provider. The deprecated "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"duration_seconds"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"units_billed"},{"type":"text","value":" attributes carry the same quantities without the unit and remain emitted for backward compatibility."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"metrics","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Metrics"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Two GenAI-standard histograms:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"gen_ai.client.operation.duration"},{"type":"text","value":" (seconds) — recorded "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"once per "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat()"},{"type":"text","value":" call"}]},{"type":"text","value":", covering all agent-loop iterations and tool execution. On error or abort the record carries an "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"error.type"},{"type":"text","value":" attribute (the thrown error's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"name"},{"type":"text","value":", or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"\"cancelled\""},{"type":"text","value":" for aborts)."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"gen_ai.client.token.usage"},{"type":"text","value":" (tokens) — recorded "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"once per iteration"}]},{"type":"text","value":" (two records: input and output), tagged with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"gen_ai.token.type"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Both "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"gen_ai.response.id"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"gen_ai.response.model"},{"type":"text","value":" are deliberately excluded from metric attributes to keep cardinality low (per-request custom-model names and request IDs would blow up the series set)."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"privacy-capturing-prompts-and-completions","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Privacy: capturing prompts and completions"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"By default, only metadata lands on spans. To record prompt and completion content, set "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"captureContent: true"},{"type":"text","value":". Content is captured as OTel span events following the GenAI convention:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"gen_ai.user.message"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"gen_ai.system.message"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"gen_ai.assistant.message"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"gen_ai.tool.message"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"gen_ai.choice"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pass a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"redact"},{"type":"text","value":" function to strip PII before anything is recorded:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { otelMiddleware } from '@tanstack/ai/middlewares/otel'\nimport { trace } from '@opentelemetry/api'\n\nconst tracer = trace.getTracer('my-app')\n\notelMiddleware({\n  tracer,\n  captureContent: true,\n  redact: (text) => text.replace(/\\b\\d{3}-\\d{2}-\\d{4}\\b/g, '[SSN]'),\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"redact"},{"type":"text","value":" throws, the middleware writes the literal sentinel "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"\"[redaction_failed]\""},{"type":"text","value":" into the span event and logs a warning — it never falls back to the raw content. This is the load-bearing invariant for users who ship traces to third-party backends: a broken redactor should shut off capture, not leak prompts."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Accumulated assistant text (the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"gen_ai.choice"},{"type":"text","value":" event) is capped at "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"maxContentLength"},{"type":"text","value":" characters (default "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"100 000"},{"type":"text","value":"); longer completions are truncated with a trailing "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"\"…\""},{"type":"text","value":" marker."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Multimodal messages (images, audio, video, documents) keep their parts in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"gen_ai.input.messages"},{"type":"text","value":", in the OTel GenAI part shapes:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Text: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ \"type\": \"text\", \"content\": \"...\" }"},{"type":"text","value":". "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"redact"},{"type":"text","value":" runs on it."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"URL source: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ \"type\": \"uri\", \"modality\": \"image\", \"uri\": \"https://...\", \"mime_type\": \"image/png\" }"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Provider file handle: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ \"type\": \"file\", \"modality\": \"image\", \"file_id\": \"...\" }"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Inline base64 data or a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"data:"},{"type":"text","value":" URL: a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"[image]"},{"type":"text","value":" text placeholder, so the bytes do not go onto the span."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Span events stay flat strings, with the same placeholders for every media part ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"look at this [image]"},{"type":"text","value":")."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Prompt/system/user message events fire from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onConfig"},{"type":"text","value":" at the start of every iteration, which means the full conversation history (as the adapter will re-send it) is re-emitted on each iteration span. This mirrors what the provider actually sees on the wire."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"extension-points","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Extension points"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"All four extensions are optional. Each wraps user code in try/catch — a thrown callback becomes a log line, never a broken chat."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"spannameformatter-info","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"spanNameFormatter(info)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Override default span names. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"info.kind"},{"type":"text","value":" is "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'chat' | 'iteration' | 'tool'"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { otelMiddleware } from '@tanstack/ai/middlewares/otel'\nimport { trace } from '@opentelemetry/api'\n\nconst tracer = trace.getTracer('my-app')\n\notelMiddleware({\n  tracer,\n  spanNameFormatter: (info) =>\n    info.kind === 'tool' ? `tool:${info.toolName}` : `chat:${info.ctx.model}`,\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"attributeenricher-info","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"attributeEnricher(info)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Add custom attributes to every span. Fires once per span."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { otelMiddleware } from '@tanstack/ai/middlewares/otel'\nimport { trace } from '@opentelemetry/api'\nimport { getCurrentTenant } from './context'\n\nconst tracer = trace.getTracer('my-app')\n\notelMiddleware({\n  tracer,\n  attributeEnricher: () => ({\n    'tenant.id': getCurrentTenant(),\n  }),\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"onbeforespanstart-info-options","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onBeforeSpanStart(info, options)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Mutate "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"SpanOptions"},{"type":"text","value":" immediately before "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tracer.startSpan(...)"},{"type":"text","value":". Useful for adding links, custom start times, or extra default attributes."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"onspanend-info-span","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onSpanEnd(info, span)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Fires just before every "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"span.end()"},{"type":"text","value":". Common uses: record custom events, emit per-tool metrics via your own "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Meter"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { otelMiddleware } from '@tanstack/ai/middlewares/otel'\nimport { trace, metrics } from '@opentelemetry/api'\n\nconst tracer = trace.getTracer('my-app')\nconst meter = metrics.getMeter('my-app')\n\nconst toolDuration = meter.createHistogram('tool.duration')\notelMiddleware({\n  tracer,\n  onSpanEnd: (info, span) => {\n    if (info.kind === 'tool') {\n      // span is still recording; read timestamps from your own store if needed\n      toolDuration.record(1, { 'tool.name': info.toolName })\n    }\n  },\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"beyond-chat-media-activities","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Beyond chat: media activities"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"otelMiddleware"},{"type":"text","value":" is not chat-only. The media activities ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"generateImage"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"generateVideo"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"generateLiveVideo"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"generateWorld"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"generateAudio"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"generateSpeech"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"generateTranscription"},{"type":"text","value":") accept the "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"same"}]},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"otelMiddleware"},{"type":"text","value":" value on their "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"middleware"},{"type":"text","value":" option. Each is a single request to response (or submit then poll for video), so the middleware emits one span per call instead of the chat span tree:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { generateImage } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { otelMiddleware } from '@tanstack/ai/middlewares/otel'\nimport { openaiImage } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\nimport { trace, metrics } from '@opentelemetry/api'\n\nconst otel = otelMiddleware({\n  tracer: trace.getTracer('my-app'),\n  meter: metrics.getMeter('my-app'),\n})\n\nconst result = await generateImage({\n  adapter: openaiImage('gpt-image-2'),\n  prompt: 'A serene mountain landscape at sunset',\n  middleware: [otel],\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You can pass the same "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"otel"},{"type":"text","value":" value to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat()"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"decide()"},{"type":"text","value":", and any media activity. Its shared lifecycle hooks ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onStart"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onUsage"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onFinish"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onAbort"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onError"},{"type":"text","value":") are authored against the activity-agnostic "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"GenerationMiddlewareContext"},{"type":"text","value":", so the one instance works everywhere."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Each media call produces one "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"CLIENT"},{"type":"text","value":" span tagged with the activity's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"gen_ai.operation.name"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Activity"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"gen_ai.operation.name"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"generateImage"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"image_generation"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"generateVideo"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"video_generation"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"generateAudio"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"audio_generation"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"generateSpeech"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"text_to_speech"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"generateTranscription"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"transcription"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"generateWorld"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"world_generation"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"generateLiveVideo"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"live_video_generation"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"summarize"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"summarize"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"decide"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"evaluate"}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The span carries "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"gen_ai.system"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"gen_ai.request.model"},{"type":"text","value":" at start and, on finish, the same "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"gen_ai.usage.*"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tanstack.ai.usage.*"},{"type":"text","value":" attributes documented above — including the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tanstack.ai.usage.billed_quantity"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tanstack.ai.usage.billed_unit"},{"type":"text","value":" pair for unit-billed media. When a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Meter"},{"type":"text","value":" is supplied it records the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"gen_ai.client.operation.duration"},{"type":"text","value":" histogram, tagged per activity. For streaming video the span covers the full create → poll → complete lifecycle. Non-streaming video is two calls, so the submit itself emits no span — the run opens once the provider accepts the job, and the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getVideoJobStatus()"},{"type":"text","value":" poll that observes a terminal state ends it. If a streaming video consumer abandons the stream before completion, the span is ended via "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onAbort"},{"type":"text","value":" (status "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ERROR"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tanstack.ai.completion.reason = cancelled"},{"type":"text","value":") rather than leaked."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"otelMiddleware"},{"type":"text","value":" applies the same "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"spanNameFormatter"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"attributeEnricher"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onBeforeSpanStart"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onSpanEnd"},{"type":"text","value":" extension points to media spans — the span info is discriminated by "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"kind"},{"type":"text","value":", where media spans report "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"kind: 'generation'"},{"type":"text","value":". For a custom backend, implement the base "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"GenerationMiddleware"},{"type":"text","value":" contract directly; its hooks ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onStart"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onUsage"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onFinish"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onAbort"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onError"},{"type":"text","value":") receive the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"GenerationMiddlewareContext"},{"type":"text","value":" and fire for every activity, chat included. The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"GenerationMiddleware"},{"type":"text","value":" types are exported from the package root, while the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"otelMiddleware"},{"type":"text","value":" value lives on the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai/middlewares/otel"},{"type":"text","value":" subpath so importing "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai"},{"type":"text","value":" never requires the optional "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@opentelemetry/api"},{"type":"text","value":" peer."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"capturing-media-content","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Capturing media content"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Set "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"captureContent: true"},{"type":"text","value":" to record what a media call was asked for and what came back. The media span then gets the same attributes as a chat iteration span:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"gen_ai.input.messages"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"langfuse.observation.input"},{"type":"text","value":": one "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"user"},{"type":"text","value":" message. It holds the prompt as a text part and each input image, video, or audio as a part. For "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"generateSpeech"},{"type":"text","value":" it holds the text to speak. For "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"generateTranscription"},{"type":"text","value":" it holds the source audio."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"gen_ai.output.messages"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"langfuse.observation.output"},{"type":"text","value":": one "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"assistant"},{"type":"text","value":" message. It holds each generated image, audio, or video URL as a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"uri"},{"type":"text","value":" part. For "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"generateTranscription"},{"type":"text","value":" it holds the transcript as a text part."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Media parts use the part shapes from "},{"type":"link","href":"#privacy-capturing-prompts-and-completions","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Privacy: capturing prompts and completions"}]},{"type":"text","value":". A URL becomes "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ \"type\": \"uri\", \"modality\": \"image\", \"uri\": \"https://...\" }"},{"type":"text","value":". Inline data never goes onto the span. Base64 output, a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"data:"},{"type":"text","value":" URL, a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"File"},{"type":"text","value":", or a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Blob"},{"type":"text","value":" becomes a text placeholder such as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"[image]"},{"type":"text","value":". "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"redact"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"maxContentLength"},{"type":"text","value":" apply to each text part."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For non-streaming video, the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getVideoJobStatus()"},{"type":"text","value":" span has the output URL but not the prompt. Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"generateVideo({ stream: true })"},{"type":"text","value":" to get both on one span."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"related","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Related"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./middleware","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Middleware"}]},{"type":"text","value":" — the lifecycle this middleware hooks into"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./debug-logging","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Debug Logging"}]},{"type":"text","value":" — quick console-output diagnostics, complementary to OTel"}]}]}]}],"headings":[{"id":"setup","text":"Setup","level":2},{"id":"what-gets-emitted","text":"What gets emitted","level":2},{"id":"spans","text":"Spans","level":3},{"id":"attribute-reference","text":"Attribute reference","level":3},{"id":"metrics","text":"Metrics","level":3},{"id":"privacy-capturing-prompts-and-completions","text":"Privacy: capturing prompts and completions","level":2},{"id":"extension-points","text":"Extension points","level":2},{"id":"spannameformatter-info","text":"spanNameFormatter(info)","level":3},{"id":"attributeenricher-info","text":"attributeEnricher(info)","level":3},{"id":"onbeforespanstart-info-options","text":"onBeforeSpanStart(info, options)","level":3},{"id":"onspanend-info-span","text":"onSpanEnd(info, span)","level":3},{"id":"beyond-chat-media-activities","text":"Beyond chat: media activities","level":2},{"id":"capturing-media-content","text":"Capturing media content","level":3},{"id":"related","text":"Related","level":2}]},"frameworks":["react","vue","solid","svelte","preact","angular","vanilla","octane"],"downloadMarkdown":"\nThe `otelMiddleware` factory wires TanStack AI into your existing OpenTelemetry setup. Every `chat()` call produces a root span, one child span per provider model call (agent-loop turn **or** structured-output finalization), and one grandchild span per tool call — all with [GenAI semantic-convention attributes](https://opentelemetry.io/docs/specs/semconv/gen-ai/). It also records GenAI token and duration histograms when a `Meter` is provided.\n\nStructured-output calls with no tools skip the agent loop and only run the finalization request. That path still opens an iteration span (via the `structuredOutput` middleware phase) so backends that key off generation spans (e.g. PostHog `$ai_generation`) and `captureContent` both work. Native combined mode (`supportsCombinedToolsAndSchema`) does not fire that phase — the single `beforeModel` span covers the combined call.\n\n## Setup\n\nInstall `@opentelemetry/api` — it's an optional peer dependency of `@tanstack/ai`:\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"package-manager\" mode=\"install\" -->\n\nreact: @opentelemetry/api\nvue: @opentelemetry/api\nsolid: @opentelemetry/api\nsvelte: @opentelemetry/api\npreact: @opentelemetry/api\nangular: @opentelemetry/api\nvanilla: @opentelemetry/api\noctane: @opentelemetry/api\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\nWire up your OTel SDK however you already do (e.g. `@opentelemetry/sdk-node`). Then pass a `Tracer` (and optionally a `Meter`) into the middleware. The OTel middleware lives on its own subpath — importing it never affects users who don't need OTel:\n\n```ts\nimport { chat } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { otelMiddleware } from '@tanstack/ai/middlewares/otel'\nimport { openaiText } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\nimport { trace, metrics } from '@opentelemetry/api'\n\nconst otel = otelMiddleware({\n  tracer: trace.getTracer('my-app'),\n  meter: metrics.getMeter('my-app'),\n})\n\nconst { text } = await chat({\n  adapter: openaiText('gpt-5.5'),\n  messages: [{ role: 'user', content: 'hi' }],\n  middleware: [otel],\n  stream: false,\n})\n```\n\n## What gets emitted\n\n### Spans\n\n```text\nchat gpt-5.5              (root, kind: INTERNAL)\n├── chat gpt-5.5 #0       (iteration, kind: CLIENT)\n│   ├── execute_tool get_weather\n│   └── execute_tool get_time\n└── chat gpt-5.5 #1       (iteration, kind: CLIENT)\n```\n\nIteration spans are numbered (`#0`, `#1`, ...) in the order model calls are observed, so distinct provider round-trips of the same chat are easy to pick apart in trace viewers.\n\n### Attribute reference\n\n| Level | Attribute | Value |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| root / iteration | `gen_ai.system` | `openai`, `anthropic`, ... |\n| iteration | `gen_ai.operation.name` | `chat` |\n| root / iteration | `gen_ai.request.model` | requested model |\n| iteration | `gen_ai.response.model` | actual model |\n| iteration | `gen_ai.request.temperature` | from config |\n| iteration | `gen_ai.request.top_p` | from config |\n| iteration | `gen_ai.request.max_tokens` | from config |\n| iteration | `gen_ai.usage.input_tokens` | per iteration |\n| iteration | `gen_ai.usage.output_tokens` | per iteration |\n| root / iteration | `gen_ai.usage.total_tokens` | provider-reported total |\n| root / iteration | `gen_ai.usage.cost` | provider-reported cost, when available |\n| root / iteration | `gen_ai.usage.cache_read.input_tokens` | cached prompt tokens, when reported |\n| root / iteration | `gen_ai.usage.cache_creation.input_tokens` | cache-write prompt tokens, when reported |\n| root / iteration | `gen_ai.usage.reasoning.output_tokens` | reasoning/thinking tokens, when reported |\n| root / iteration | `tanstack.ai.usage.billed_quantity` | non-token billed quantity, when reported |\n| root / iteration | `tanstack.ai.usage.billed_unit` | unit of the billed quantity (`seconds`, `units`, ...) |\n| root / iteration | `tanstack.ai.usage.duration_seconds` | deprecated duration count; read `billed_quantity`/`billed_unit` instead |\n| root / iteration | `tanstack.ai.usage.units_billed` | deprecated bare unit count; read `billed_quantity`/`billed_unit` instead |\n| root / iteration | `tanstack.ai.usage.upstream_cost` | gateway upstream cost (e.g. OpenRouter), when reported |\n| root / iteration | `tanstack.ai.usage.upstream_input_cost` | upstream input cost split, when reported |\n| root / iteration | `tanstack.ai.usage.upstream_output_cost` | upstream output cost split, when reported |\n| iteration | `gen_ai.response.finish_reasons` | `[stop]`, `[tool_calls]`, ... |\n| root | `gen_ai.usage.input_tokens` | rolled up |\n| root | `gen_ai.usage.output_tokens` | rolled up |\n| root | `tanstack.ai.iterations` | iteration count |\n| tool | `gen_ai.tool.name` | tool name |\n| tool | `gen_ai.tool.call.id` | tool call id |\n| tool | `gen_ai.tool.type` | `function` |\n| tool | `tanstack.ai.tool.outcome` | `success` / `error` |\n\nUsage attributes beyond input/output tokens are emitted only when the provider reports them, so spans stay clean otherwise. Cache and reasoning breakdowns use the official GenAI semconv names; `gen_ai.usage.cost` and `gen_ai.usage.total_tokens` are de-facto extensions consumed directly by backends like PostHog — without them, backends re-derive cost from their own price tables and lose cache discounts and gateway markup. Fields with no established convention (the billed quantity/unit pair, the upstream cost split, and the deprecated bare counts) are TanStack-namespaced.\n\nFor non-token billing (seconds of video or transcription, fal's endpoint units, ...), `tanstack.ai.usage.billed_quantity` and `tanstack.ai.usage.billed_unit` are emitted as a pair from `usage.billed`, so backends can label and aggregate media usage without knowing the provider. The deprecated `duration_seconds` / `units_billed` attributes carry the same quantities without the unit and remain emitted for backward compatibility.\n\n### Metrics\n\nTwo GenAI-standard histograms:\n\n- `gen_ai.client.operation.duration` (seconds) — recorded **once per `chat()` call**, covering all agent-loop iterations and tool execution. On error or abort the record carries an `error.type` attribute (the thrown error's `name`, or `\"cancelled\"` for aborts).\n- `gen_ai.client.token.usage` (tokens) — recorded **once per iteration** (two records: input and output), tagged with `gen_ai.token.type`.\n\nBoth `gen_ai.response.id` and `gen_ai.response.model` are deliberately excluded from metric attributes to keep cardinality low (per-request custom-model names and request IDs would blow up the series set).\n\n## Privacy: capturing prompts and completions\n\nBy default, only metadata lands on spans. To record prompt and completion content, set `captureContent: true`. Content is captured as OTel span events following the GenAI convention:\n\n- `gen_ai.user.message`, `gen_ai.system.message`, `gen_ai.assistant.message`, `gen_ai.tool.message`, `gen_ai.choice`\n\nPass a `redact` function to strip PII before anything is recorded:\n\n```ts\nimport { otelMiddleware } from '@tanstack/ai/middlewares/otel'\nimport { trace } from '@opentelemetry/api'\n\nconst tracer = trace.getTracer('my-app')\n\notelMiddleware({\n  tracer,\n  captureContent: true,\n  redact: (text) => text.replace(/\\b\\d{3}-\\d{2}-\\d{4}\\b/g, '[SSN]'),\n})\n```\n\nIf `redact` throws, the middleware writes the literal sentinel `\"[redaction_failed]\"` into the span event and logs a warning — it never falls back to the raw content. This is the load-bearing invariant for users who ship traces to third-party backends: a broken redactor should shut off capture, not leak prompts.\n\nAccumulated assistant text (the `gen_ai.choice` event) is capped at `maxContentLength` characters (default `100 000`); longer completions are truncated with a trailing `\"…\"` marker.\n\nMultimodal messages (images, audio, video, documents) keep their parts in `gen_ai.input.messages`, in the OTel GenAI part shapes:\n\n- Text: `{ \"type\": \"text\", \"content\": \"...\" }`. `redact` runs on it.\n- URL source: `{ \"type\": \"uri\", \"modality\": \"image\", \"uri\": \"https://...\", \"mime_type\": \"image/png\" }`.\n- Provider file handle: `{ \"type\": \"file\", \"modality\": \"image\", \"file_id\": \"...\" }`.\n- Inline base64 data or a `data:` URL: a `[image]` text placeholder, so the bytes do not go onto the span.\n\nSpan events stay flat strings, with the same placeholders for every media part (`look at this [image]`).\n\nPrompt/system/user message events fire from `onConfig` at the start of every iteration, which means the full conversation history (as the adapter will re-send it) is re-emitted on each iteration span. This mirrors what the provider actually sees on the wire.\n\n## Extension points\n\nAll four extensions are optional. Each wraps user code in try/catch — a thrown callback becomes a log line, never a broken chat.\n\n### `spanNameFormatter(info)`\n\nOverride default span names. `info.kind` is `'chat' | 'iteration' | 'tool'`.\n\n```ts\nimport { otelMiddleware } from '@tanstack/ai/middlewares/otel'\nimport { trace } from '@opentelemetry/api'\n\nconst tracer = trace.getTracer('my-app')\n\notelMiddleware({\n  tracer,\n  spanNameFormatter: (info) =>\n    info.kind === 'tool' ? `tool:${info.toolName}` : `chat:${info.ctx.model}`,\n})\n```\n\n### `attributeEnricher(info)`\n\nAdd custom attributes to every span. Fires once per span.\n\n```ts\nimport { otelMiddleware } from '@tanstack/ai/middlewares/otel'\nimport { trace } from '@opentelemetry/api'\nimport { getCurrentTenant } from './context'\n\nconst tracer = trace.getTracer('my-app')\n\notelMiddleware({\n  tracer,\n  attributeEnricher: () => ({\n    'tenant.id': getCurrentTenant(),\n  }),\n})\n```\n\n### `onBeforeSpanStart(info, options)`\n\nMutate `SpanOptions` immediately before `tracer.startSpan(...)`. Useful for adding links, custom start times, or extra default attributes.\n\n### `onSpanEnd(info, span)`\n\nFires just before every `span.end()`. Common uses: record custom events, emit per-tool metrics via your own `Meter`.\n\n```ts\nimport { otelMiddleware } from '@tanstack/ai/middlewares/otel'\nimport { trace, metrics } from '@opentelemetry/api'\n\nconst tracer = trace.getTracer('my-app')\nconst meter = metrics.getMeter('my-app')\n\nconst toolDuration = meter.createHistogram('tool.duration')\notelMiddleware({\n  tracer,\n  onSpanEnd: (info, span) => {\n    if (info.kind === 'tool') {\n      // span is still recording; read timestamps from your own store if needed\n      toolDuration.record(1, { 'tool.name': info.toolName })\n    }\n  },\n})\n```\n\n## Beyond chat: media activities\n\n`otelMiddleware` is not chat-only. The media activities (`generateImage`, `generateVideo`, `generateLiveVideo`, `generateWorld`, `generateAudio`, `generateSpeech`, and `generateTranscription`) accept the **same** `otelMiddleware` value on their `middleware` option. Each is a single request to response (or submit then poll for video), so the middleware emits one span per call instead of the chat span tree:\n\n```ts\nimport { generateImage } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { otelMiddleware } from '@tanstack/ai/middlewares/otel'\nimport { openaiImage } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\nimport { trace, metrics } from '@opentelemetry/api'\n\nconst otel = otelMiddleware({\n  tracer: trace.getTracer('my-app'),\n  meter: metrics.getMeter('my-app'),\n})\n\nconst result = await generateImage({\n  adapter: openaiImage('gpt-image-2'),\n  prompt: 'A serene mountain landscape at sunset',\n  middleware: [otel],\n})\n```\n\nYou can pass the same `otel` value to `chat()`, `decide()`, and any media activity. Its shared lifecycle hooks (`onStart` / `onUsage` / `onFinish` / `onAbort` / `onError`) are authored against the activity-agnostic `GenerationMiddlewareContext`, so the one instance works everywhere.\n\nEach media call produces one `CLIENT` span tagged with the activity's `gen_ai.operation.name`:\n\n| Activity | `gen_ai.operation.name` |\n| --- | --- |\n| `generateImage` | `image_generation` |\n| `generateVideo` | `video_generation` |\n| `generateAudio` | `audio_generation` |\n| `generateSpeech` | `text_to_speech` |\n| `generateTranscription` | `transcription` |\n| `generateWorld` | `world_generation` |\n| `generateLiveVideo` | `live_video_generation` |\n| `summarize` | `summarize` |\n| `decide` | `evaluate` |\n\nThe span carries `gen_ai.system` and `gen_ai.request.model` at start and, on finish, the same `gen_ai.usage.*` / `tanstack.ai.usage.*` attributes documented above — including the `tanstack.ai.usage.billed_quantity` / `tanstack.ai.usage.billed_unit` pair for unit-billed media. When a `Meter` is supplied it records the `gen_ai.client.operation.duration` histogram, tagged per activity. For streaming video the span covers the full create → poll → complete lifecycle. Non-streaming video is two calls, so the submit itself emits no span — the run opens once the provider accepts the job, and the `getVideoJobStatus()` poll that observes a terminal state ends it. If a streaming video consumer abandons the stream before completion, the span is ended via `onAbort` (status `ERROR`, `tanstack.ai.completion.reason = cancelled`) rather than leaked.\n\n`otelMiddleware` applies the same `spanNameFormatter`, `attributeEnricher`, `onBeforeSpanStart`, and `onSpanEnd` extension points to media spans — the span info is discriminated by `kind`, where media spans report `kind: 'generation'`. For a custom backend, implement the base `GenerationMiddleware` contract directly; its hooks (`onStart` / `onUsage` / `onFinish` / `onAbort` / `onError`) receive the `GenerationMiddlewareContext` and fire for every activity, chat included. The `GenerationMiddleware` types are exported from the package root, while the `otelMiddleware` value lives on the `@tanstack/ai/middlewares/otel` subpath so importing `@tanstack/ai` never requires the optional `@opentelemetry/api` peer.\n\n### Capturing media content\n\nSet `captureContent: true` to record what a media call was asked for and what came back. The media span then gets the same attributes as a chat iteration span:\n\n- `gen_ai.input.messages` and `langfuse.observation.input`: one `user` message. It holds the prompt as a text part and each input image, video, or audio as a part. For `generateSpeech` it holds the text to speak. For `generateTranscription` it holds the source audio.\n- `gen_ai.output.messages` and `langfuse.observation.output`: one `assistant` message. It holds each generated image, audio, or video URL as a `uri` part. For `generateTranscription` it holds the transcript as a text part.\n\nMedia parts use the part shapes from [Privacy: capturing prompts and completions](#privacy-capturing-prompts-and-completions). A URL becomes `{ \"type\": \"uri\", \"modality\": \"image\", \"uri\": \"https://...\" }`. Inline data never goes onto the span. Base64 output, a `data:` URL, a `File`, or a `Blob` becomes a text placeholder such as `[image]`. `redact` and `maxContentLength` apply to each text part.\n\nFor non-streaming video, the `getVideoJobStatus()` span has the output URL but not the prompt. Use `generateVideo({ stream: true })` to get both on one span.\n\n## Related\n\n- [Middleware](./middleware) — the lifecycle this middleware hooks into\n- [Debug Logging](./debug-logging) — quick console-output diagnostics, complementary to OTel","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: OpenTelemetry\nid: otel\norder: 3\ndescription: \"Emit vendor-neutral OpenTelemetry traces and metrics from every TanStack AI chat() call, following the OTel GenAI semantic conventions.\"\nkeywords:\n  - tanstack ai\n  - opentelemetry\n  - otel\n  - observability\n  - tracing\n  - metrics\n  - gen_ai\n  - semantic conventions\n---\n\nThe `otelMiddleware` factory wires TanStack AI into your existing OpenTelemetry setup. Every `chat()` call produces a root span, one child span per provider model call (agent-loop turn **or** structured-output finalization), and one grandchild span per tool call — all with [GenAI semantic-convention attributes](https://opentelemetry.io/docs/specs/semconv/gen-ai/). It also records GenAI token and duration histograms when a `Meter` is provided.\n\nStructured-output calls with no tools skip the agent loop and only run the finalization request. That path still opens an iteration span (via the `structuredOutput` middleware phase) so backends that key off generation spans (e.g. PostHog `$ai_generation`) and `captureContent` both work. Native combined mode (`supportsCombinedToolsAndSchema`) does not fire that phase — the single `beforeModel` span covers the combined call.\n\n## Setup\n\nInstall `@opentelemetry/api` — it's an optional peer dependency of `@tanstack/ai`:\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"package-manager\" mode=\"install\" -->\n\nreact: @opentelemetry/api\nvue: @opentelemetry/api\nsolid: @opentelemetry/api\nsvelte: @opentelemetry/api\npreact: @opentelemetry/api\nangular: @opentelemetry/api\nvanilla: @opentelemetry/api\noctane: @opentelemetry/api\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\nWire up your OTel SDK however you already do (e.g. `@opentelemetry/sdk-node`). Then pass a `Tracer` (and optionally a `Meter`) into the middleware. The OTel middleware lives on its own subpath — importing it never affects users who don't need OTel:\n\n```ts\nimport { chat } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { otelMiddleware } from '@tanstack/ai/middlewares/otel'\nimport { openaiText } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\nimport { trace, metrics } from '@opentelemetry/api'\n\nconst otel = otelMiddleware({\n  tracer: trace.getTracer('my-app'),\n  meter: metrics.getMeter('my-app'),\n})\n\nconst { text } = await chat({\n  adapter: openaiText('gpt-5.5'),\n  messages: [{ role: 'user', content: 'hi' }],\n  middleware: [otel],\n  stream: false,\n})\n```\n\n## What gets emitted\n\n### Spans\n\n```text\nchat gpt-5.5              (root, kind: INTERNAL)\n├── chat gpt-5.5 #0       (iteration, kind: CLIENT)\n│   ├── execute_tool get_weather\n│   └── execute_tool get_time\n└── chat gpt-5.5 #1       (iteration, kind: CLIENT)\n```\n\nIteration spans are numbered (`#0`, `#1`, ...) in the order model calls are observed, so distinct provider round-trips of the same chat are easy to pick apart in trace viewers.\n\n### Attribute reference\n\n| Level | Attribute | Value |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| root / iteration | `gen_ai.system` | `openai`, `anthropic`, ... |\n| iteration | `gen_ai.operation.name` | `chat` |\n| root / iteration | `gen_ai.request.model` | requested model |\n| iteration | `gen_ai.response.model` | actual model |\n| iteration | `gen_ai.request.temperature` | from config |\n| iteration | `gen_ai.request.top_p` | from config |\n| iteration | `gen_ai.request.max_tokens` | from config |\n| iteration | `gen_ai.usage.input_tokens` | per iteration |\n| iteration | `gen_ai.usage.output_tokens` | per iteration |\n| root / iteration | `gen_ai.usage.total_tokens` | provider-reported total |\n| root / iteration | `gen_ai.usage.cost` | provider-reported cost, when available |\n| root / iteration | `gen_ai.usage.cache_read.input_tokens` | cached prompt tokens, when reported |\n| root / iteration | `gen_ai.usage.cache_creation.input_tokens` | cache-write prompt tokens, when reported |\n| root / iteration | `gen_ai.usage.reasoning.output_tokens` | reasoning/thinking tokens, when reported |\n| root / iteration | `tanstack.ai.usage.billed_quantity` | non-token billed quantity, when reported |\n| root / iteration | `tanstack.ai.usage.billed_unit` | unit of the billed quantity (`seconds`, `units`, ...) |\n| root / iteration | `tanstack.ai.usage.duration_seconds` | deprecated duration count; read `billed_quantity`/`billed_unit` instead |\n| root / iteration | `tanstack.ai.usage.units_billed` | deprecated bare unit count; read `billed_quantity`/`billed_unit` instead |\n| root / iteration | `tanstack.ai.usage.upstream_cost` | gateway upstream cost (e.g. OpenRouter), when reported |\n| root / iteration | `tanstack.ai.usage.upstream_input_cost` | upstream input cost split, when reported |\n| root / iteration | `tanstack.ai.usage.upstream_output_cost` | upstream output cost split, when reported |\n| iteration | `gen_ai.response.finish_reasons` | `[stop]`, `[tool_calls]`, ... |\n| root | `gen_ai.usage.input_tokens` | rolled up |\n| root | `gen_ai.usage.output_tokens` | rolled up |\n| root | `tanstack.ai.iterations` | iteration count |\n| tool | `gen_ai.tool.name` | tool name |\n| tool | `gen_ai.tool.call.id` | tool call id |\n| tool | `gen_ai.tool.type` | `function` |\n| tool | `tanstack.ai.tool.outcome` | `success` / `error` |\n\nUsage attributes beyond input/output tokens are emitted only when the provider reports them, so spans stay clean otherwise. Cache and reasoning breakdowns use the official GenAI semconv names; `gen_ai.usage.cost` and `gen_ai.usage.total_tokens` are de-facto extensions consumed directly by backends like PostHog — without them, backends re-derive cost from their own price tables and lose cache discounts and gateway markup. Fields with no established convention (the billed quantity/unit pair, the upstream cost split, and the deprecated bare counts) are TanStack-namespaced.\n\nFor non-token billing (seconds of video or transcription, fal's endpoint units, ...), `tanstack.ai.usage.billed_quantity` and `tanstack.ai.usage.billed_unit` are emitted as a pair from `usage.billed`, so backends can label and aggregate media usage without knowing the provider. The deprecated `duration_seconds` / `units_billed` attributes carry the same quantities without the unit and remain emitted for backward compatibility.\n\n### Metrics\n\nTwo GenAI-standard histograms:\n\n- `gen_ai.client.operation.duration` (seconds) — recorded **once per `chat()` call**, covering all agent-loop iterations and tool execution. On error or abort the record carries an `error.type` attribute (the thrown error's `name`, or `\"cancelled\"` for aborts).\n- `gen_ai.client.token.usage` (tokens) — recorded **once per iteration** (two records: input and output), tagged with `gen_ai.token.type`.\n\nBoth `gen_ai.response.id` and `gen_ai.response.model` are deliberately excluded from metric attributes to keep cardinality low (per-request custom-model names and request IDs would blow up the series set).\n\n## Privacy: capturing prompts and completions\n\nBy default, only metadata lands on spans. To record prompt and completion content, set `captureContent: true`. Content is captured as OTel span events following the GenAI convention:\n\n- `gen_ai.user.message`, `gen_ai.system.message`, `gen_ai.assistant.message`, `gen_ai.tool.message`, `gen_ai.choice`\n\nPass a `redact` function to strip PII before anything is recorded:\n\n```ts\nimport { otelMiddleware } from '@tanstack/ai/middlewares/otel'\nimport { trace } from '@opentelemetry/api'\n\nconst tracer = trace.getTracer('my-app')\n\notelMiddleware({\n  tracer,\n  captureContent: true,\n  redact: (text) => text.replace(/\\b\\d{3}-\\d{2}-\\d{4}\\b/g, '[SSN]'),\n})\n```\n\nIf `redact` throws, the middleware writes the literal sentinel `\"[redaction_failed]\"` into the span event and logs a warning — it never falls back to the raw content. This is the load-bearing invariant for users who ship traces to third-party backends: a broken redactor should shut off capture, not leak prompts.\n\nAccumulated assistant text (the `gen_ai.choice` event) is capped at `maxContentLength` characters (default `100 000`); longer completions are truncated with a trailing `\"…\"` marker.\n\nMultimodal messages (images, audio, video, documents) keep their parts in `gen_ai.input.messages`, in the OTel GenAI part shapes:\n\n- Text: `{ \"type\": \"text\", \"content\": \"...\" }`. `redact` runs on it.\n- URL source: `{ \"type\": \"uri\", \"modality\": \"image\", \"uri\": \"https://...\", \"mime_type\": \"image/png\" }`.\n- Provider file handle: `{ \"type\": \"file\", \"modality\": \"image\", \"file_id\": \"...\" }`.\n- Inline base64 data or a `data:` URL: a `[image]` text placeholder, so the bytes do not go onto the span.\n\nSpan events stay flat strings, with the same placeholders for every media part (`look at this [image]`).\n\nPrompt/system/user message events fire from `onConfig` at the start of every iteration, which means the full conversation history (as the adapter will re-send it) is re-emitted on each iteration span. This mirrors what the provider actually sees on the wire.\n\n## Extension points\n\nAll four extensions are optional. Each wraps user code in try/catch — a thrown callback becomes a log line, never a broken chat.\n\n### `spanNameFormatter(info)`\n\nOverride default span names. `info.kind` is `'chat' | 'iteration' | 'tool'`.\n\n```ts\nimport { otelMiddleware } from '@tanstack/ai/middlewares/otel'\nimport { trace } from '@opentelemetry/api'\n\nconst tracer = trace.getTracer('my-app')\n\notelMiddleware({\n  tracer,\n  spanNameFormatter: (info) =>\n    info.kind === 'tool' ? `tool:${info.toolName}` : `chat:${info.ctx.model}`,\n})\n```\n\n### `attributeEnricher(info)`\n\nAdd custom attributes to every span. Fires once per span.\n\n```ts\nimport { otelMiddleware } from '@tanstack/ai/middlewares/otel'\nimport { trace } from '@opentelemetry/api'\nimport { getCurrentTenant } from './context'\n\nconst tracer = trace.getTracer('my-app')\n\notelMiddleware({\n  tracer,\n  attributeEnricher: () => ({\n    'tenant.id': getCurrentTenant(),\n  }),\n})\n```\n\n### `onBeforeSpanStart(info, options)`\n\nMutate `SpanOptions` immediately before `tracer.startSpan(...)`. Useful for adding links, custom start times, or extra default attributes.\n\n### `onSpanEnd(info, span)`\n\nFires just before every `span.end()`. Common uses: record custom events, emit per-tool metrics via your own `Meter`.\n\n```ts\nimport { otelMiddleware } from '@tanstack/ai/middlewares/otel'\nimport { trace, metrics } from '@opentelemetry/api'\n\nconst tracer = trace.getTracer('my-app')\nconst meter = metrics.getMeter('my-app')\n\nconst toolDuration = meter.createHistogram('tool.duration')\notelMiddleware({\n  tracer,\n  onSpanEnd: (info, span) => {\n    if (info.kind === 'tool') {\n      // span is still recording; read timestamps from your own store if needed\n      toolDuration.record(1, { 'tool.name': info.toolName })\n    }\n  },\n})\n```\n\n## Beyond chat: media activities\n\n`otelMiddleware` is not chat-only. The media activities (`generateImage`, `generateVideo`, `generateLiveVideo`, `generateWorld`, `generateAudio`, `generateSpeech`, and `generateTranscription`) accept the **same** `otelMiddleware` value on their `middleware` option. Each is a single request to response (or submit then poll for video), so the middleware emits one span per call instead of the chat span tree:\n\n```ts\nimport { generateImage } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { otelMiddleware } from '@tanstack/ai/middlewares/otel'\nimport { openaiImage } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\nimport { trace, metrics } from '@opentelemetry/api'\n\nconst otel = otelMiddleware({\n  tracer: trace.getTracer('my-app'),\n  meter: metrics.getMeter('my-app'),\n})\n\nconst result = await generateImage({\n  adapter: openaiImage('gpt-image-2'),\n  prompt: 'A serene mountain landscape at sunset',\n  middleware: [otel],\n})\n```\n\nYou can pass the same `otel` value to `chat()`, `decide()`, and any media activity. Its shared lifecycle hooks (`onStart` / `onUsage` / `onFinish` / `onAbort` / `onError`) are authored against the activity-agnostic `GenerationMiddlewareContext`, so the one instance works everywhere.\n\nEach media call produces one `CLIENT` span tagged with the activity's `gen_ai.operation.name`:\n\n| Activity | `gen_ai.operation.name` |\n| --- | --- |\n| `generateImage` | `image_generation` |\n| `generateVideo` | `video_generation` |\n| `generateAudio` | `audio_generation` |\n| `generateSpeech` | `text_to_speech` |\n| `generateTranscription` | `transcription` |\n| `generateWorld` | `world_generation` |\n| `generateLiveVideo` | `live_video_generation` |\n| `summarize` | `summarize` |\n| `decide` | `evaluate` |\n\nThe span carries `gen_ai.system` and `gen_ai.request.model` at start and, on finish, the same `gen_ai.usage.*` / `tanstack.ai.usage.*` attributes documented above — including the `tanstack.ai.usage.billed_quantity` / `tanstack.ai.usage.billed_unit` pair for unit-billed media. When a `Meter` is supplied it records the `gen_ai.client.operation.duration` histogram, tagged per activity. For streaming video the span covers the full create → poll → complete lifecycle. Non-streaming video is two calls, so the submit itself emits no span — the run opens once the provider accepts the job, and the `getVideoJobStatus()` poll that observes a terminal state ends it. If a streaming video consumer abandons the stream before completion, the span is ended via `onAbort` (status `ERROR`, `tanstack.ai.completion.reason = cancelled`) rather than leaked.\n\n`otelMiddleware` applies the same `spanNameFormatter`, `attributeEnricher`, `onBeforeSpanStart`, and `onSpanEnd` extension points to media spans — the span info is discriminated by `kind`, where media spans report `kind: 'generation'`. For a custom backend, implement the base `GenerationMiddleware` contract directly; its hooks (`onStart` / `onUsage` / `onFinish` / `onAbort` / `onError`) receive the `GenerationMiddlewareContext` and fire for every activity, chat included. The `GenerationMiddleware` types are exported from the package root, while the `otelMiddleware` value lives on the `@tanstack/ai/middlewares/otel` subpath so importing `@tanstack/ai` never requires the optional `@opentelemetry/api` peer.\n\n### Capturing media content\n\nSet `captureContent: true` to record what a media call was asked for and what came back. The media span then gets the same attributes as a chat iteration span:\n\n- `gen_ai.input.messages` and `langfuse.observation.input`: one `user` message. It holds the prompt as a text part and each input image, video, or audio as a part. For `generateSpeech` it holds the text to speak. For `generateTranscription` it holds the source audio.\n- `gen_ai.output.messages` and `langfuse.observation.output`: one `assistant` message. It holds each generated image, audio, or video URL as a `uri` part. For `generateTranscription` it holds the transcript as a text part.\n\nMedia parts use the part shapes from [Privacy: capturing prompts and completions](#privacy-capturing-prompts-and-completions). A URL becomes `{ \"type\": \"uri\", \"modality\": \"image\", \"uri\": \"https://...\" }`. Inline data never goes onto the span. Base64 output, a `data:` URL, a `File`, or a `Blob` becomes a text placeholder such as `[image]`. `redact` and `maxContentLength` apply to each text part.\n\nFor non-streaming video, the `getVideoJobStatus()` span has the output URL but not the prompt. Use `generateVideo({ stream: true })` to get both on one span.\n\n## Related\n\n- [Middleware](./middleware) — the lifecycle this middleware hooks into\n- [Debug Logging](./debug-logging) — quick console-output diagnostics, complementary to OTel"}
